@prefix sh: <http://www.w3.org/ns/shacl#> .
@prefix orexis: <http://example.org/orexis#> .
@prefix speech: <http://example.org/orexis/speech#> .
@prefix rdfs: <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#> .
@prefix email: <http://example.org/orexis/email#> .
@prefix owl:  <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#> .
@prefix prov: <http://www.w3.org/ns/prov#> .

<> a orexis:OntologyGraph .    # this document is one graph, and this is what it is

#  OREXIS EMAIL TRANSPORT. It declares no word of the mail of its own: a mailbox it reaches is a `schema:ContactPoint` with a
#  `schema:email`, schema.org's words, and which row reads it is what points at it — the channel of a `speech:Chat`
#  is a person's prose, translation's. The agent's own mailbox — its address, its credential, its servers — is
#  `secrets/<agent>/mail.env`, environment and never a graph.


#  HOW OFTEN THE MAILBOX IS POLLED is a role's to say, in the agent's self graph, and the shape's default below where none says.

email:polledEveryS a owl:DatatypeProperty ; rdfs:label "polled every, in seconds" ;
    rdfs:comment "How often an agent's mailbox is polled, in real seconds, said of a role the agent plays that speaks through it. Thirty where no role says." .

#  WHAT HOLDS WHERE NO ROLE SAYS HOW OFTEN, read by the transport as it connects: the one place the figure lives.
[] a sh:NodeShape ;
    sh:targetClass orexis:Role ;
    sh:property [ sh:path email:polledEveryS ; sh:defaultValue 30 ] .
